  "response": "**VERDICT: REJECT**\n\n**Overall Assessment**:  \nThe `BuggyTooltip` component demonstrates a common anti-pattern: decorating an element with an ARIA role (`role=\"tooltip\"`) while omitting the foundational programmatic association, focus listeners, and keyboard dismissal mechanisms required by WAI-ARIA Authoring Practices Guide (APG) and WCAG 2.2 AA. Keyboard-only users cannot trigger the tooltip, screen reader users never receive its description upon focusing the button, and users cannot dismiss it without moving pointer focus.\n\n---\n\n### Pre-commitment Predictions\n- Tooltip triggers on hover only, missing `onFocus`/`onBlur` handlers for keyboard users.\n- Missing `aria-describedby` linking the trigger button to the tooltip container `id`.\n- Missing Escape key handler to dismiss the tooltip without shifting focus (WCAG 1.4.13 Content on Hover or Focus).\n- Tooltip content disappears when hovered if pointer moves towards it (hoverable content requirement under WCAG 1.4.13).\n\n---\n\n### Critical Findings (blocks access)\n\n1. **Missing Keyboard Triggering (`onFocus` / `onBlur`)**\n   - **Location**: Lines 8\u201311 (`<button onMouseEnter={...} onMouseLeave={...}>`)\n   - **Element**: Trigger `<button>`\n   - **Impacted Group**: Keyboard-only users, switch device users, screen magnifier users navigating via keyboard.\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.1.1 Keyboard (Level A), WAI-ARIA APG Tooltip Pattern.\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: The tooltip state is controlled exclusively by pointer events (`onMouseEnter`, `onMouseLeave`). A keyboard user tabbing to the button will never see the tooltip appear.\n   - **Fix**: Add `onFocus={() => setShowTooltip(true)}` and `onBlur={() => setShowTooltip(false)}` to the trigger `<button>`.\n\n2. **Missing Programmatic Association via `aria-describedby`**\n   - **Location**: Lines 8\u201313, Lines 14\u201320\n   - **Element**: Trigger `<button>` and Tooltip `<div>`\n   - **Impacted Group**: Screen reader users (NVDA, JAWS, VoiceOver).\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 1.3.1 Info and Relationships (Level A), WCAG 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value (Level A), WAI-ARIA APG Tooltip Pattern.\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: While the tooltip container has `role=\"tooltip\"`, there is no `id` on the tooltip or `aria-describedby` reference on the button. Screen readers focus the button and announce only `{trigger}` text, completely unaware that supplementary description exists.\n   - **Fix**: Generate a unique identifier (e.g. via React\u2019s `useId()`), set `id={tooltipId}` on the tooltip container, and add `aria-describedby={showTooltip ? tooltipId : undefined}` (or persistent association) on the `<button>`.\n\n---\n\n### Major Findings (significantly degrades experience)\n\n1. **Cannot Dismiss Tooltip Without Moving Focus (Missing Escape Key Support)**\n   - **Location**: Lines 6\u201313\n   - **Element**: Trigger `<button>` / Tooltip container\n   - **Impacted Group**: Low vision users (magnification), keyboard-only users, cognitive users.\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 1.4.13 Content on Hover or Focus (Dismissible requirement, Level AA).\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: When the tooltip opens, it may obscure adjacent content or inputs. Under WCAG 1.4.13, users must be able to dismiss additional content without moving pointer hover or keyboard focus, typically via the `Escape` key.\n   - **Fix**: Add a `keydown` handler on the trigger or document when `showTooltip` is active:\n     ```jsx\n     onKeyDown={(e) => {\n       if (e.key === 'Escape' && showTooltip) {\n         e.stopPropagation();\n         setShowTooltip(false);\n       }\n     }}\n     ```\n\n2. **Lack of Hover Persistence over Tooltip Content**\n   - **Location**: Lines 14\u201320\n   - **Element**: `<div className=\"tooltip-content\" role=\"tooltip\">`\n   - **Impacted Group**: Low vision users using screen magnifiers, motor-impaired users.\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 1.4.13 Content on Hover or Focus (Hoverable requirement, Level AA).\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: If the user moves the pointer from the trigger toward the tooltip to read it under magnification, the trigger\u2019s `onMouseLeave` fires immediately, closing the tooltip before the pointer reaches it.\n   - **Fix**: Ensure the tooltip content itself retains the hover state (e.g., placing `onMouseEnter`/`onMouseLeave` on the common parent wrapper `.tooltip-wrapper`, or adding pointer listeners to the tooltip content to maintain `showTooltip(true)`).\n\n---\n\n### Minor Findings & Enhancements\n\n- **Default Button Type Attribute (Minor)**: Lines 8\u201313 omit `type=\"button\"`. If this tooltip trigger is placed inside a `<form>`, activating it with `Enter` will inadvertently trigger form submission. Add `type=\"button\"`.\n- **Content Rendering Type (Enhancement)**: Tooltip text content passed via `{content}` should be concise plain text or simple inline formatting. If rich interactive elements (links, buttons) are passed in `{content}`, this pattern should be refactored to a **Toggletip / Non-modal Dialog (`role=\"dialog\"`)**, as interactive elements inside `role=\"tooltip\"` or `aria-describedby` are ignored or inaccessible to screen readers.\n\n---\n\n### What's Missing\n\n- **Deterministic ID Association**: No `id` on the tooltip container; no `aria-describedby` on the invoking element.\n- **Keyboard activation & dismissal**: No `onFocus`/`onBlur` listeners and no `Escape` key event handling.\n- **Pointer persistence buffer**: No event delegation or bounding strategy permitting hover transition to the tooltip content.\n\n---\n\n### Multi-Perspective Notes\n\n| Perspective | Alarm Level | Trigger Signal |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Screen reader** | **HIGH** | `role=\"tooltip\"` is present but orphaned; zero announcement or association on focus. |\n| **Keyboard-only** | **HIGH** | Component is completely unreachable via keyboard navigation (`mouseenter`/`mouseleave` only). |\n| **Low vision** | **HIGH** | Fails WCAG 1.4.13 (non-dismissible without moving focus, non-hoverable under zoom). |\n| **Cognitive** | **MEDIUM** | Content may obstruct viewing area without an intuitive cancellation mechanism (Escape). |\n| **Vestibular & motion** | **LOW** | No animations or transition triggers detected. |\n| **Auditory access** | **LOW** | No media or audio-dependent state. |\n| **Environmental contrast**| **MEDIUM** | Depends on CSS styling of `.tooltip-content` against ambient background. |\n\n- **Screen reader user**: Hears only the button text. The tooltip text is rendered conditionally in the DOM without being referenced by `aria-describedby`, making it invisible in normal reading order.\n- **Keyboard-only user**: Can tab to the button, but no tooltip ever renders.\n- **Low vision user**: If hovering over the trigger with a screen magnifier, the tooltip may block surrounding elements with no way to press `Escape` to read the obscured information.\n\n---\n\n### Remediation Blueprint\n\n```jsx\nimport React, { useState, useId } from 'react';\n\nconst AccessibleTooltip = ({ trigger, content }) => {\n  const [showTooltip, setShowTooltip] = useState(false);\n  const tooltipId = useId();\n\n  const handleKeyDown = (e) => {\n    if (e.key === 'Escape' && showTooltip) {\n      e.stopPropagation();\n      setShowTooltip(false);\n    }\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div\n      className=\"tooltip-wrapper\"\n      onMouseEnter={() => setShowTooltip(true)}\n      onMouseLeave={() => setShowTooltip(false)}\n    >\n      <button\n        type=\"button\"\n        aria-describedby={showTooltip ? tooltipId : undefined}\n        onFocus={() => setShowTooltip(true)}\n        onBlur={() => setShowTooltip(false)}\n        onKeyDown={handleKeyDown}\n      >\n        {trigger}\n      </button>\n\n      {showTooltip && (\n        <div\n          id={tooltipId}\n          className=\"tooltip-content\"\n          role=\"tooltip\"\n        >\n          {content}\n        </div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n};\n\nexport default AccessibleTooltip;\n```\n\n---\n\n### Verdict Justification\n\n**REJECT**. Although automated tooling might notice `role=\"tooltip\"` and pass basic markup linters, the component fails three Level A/AA WCAG criteria (2.1.1, 1.3.1, 1.4.13) and violates the WAI-ARIA APG Tooltip pattern. To upgrade to **ACCEPT**, the component must associate the tooltip via `aria-describedby`, render on keyboard focus (`onFocus`/`onBlur`), and support dismissibility via `Escape`.\n",
